# 10. AI BUSINESS AND TRADE COMPLIANCE SCREENING

Build a source-based Compliance Screening Agent.

The purpose is to identify potential risks, not to make unsupported accusations that a business is illegal.

Separate company screening from trade screening.

## 10.1 Company Screening

At onboarding, screen relevant information:

- Legal business name.
- Trading names and aliases.
- Country of incorporation.
- Company registration number.
- Business activities.
- Relevant ownership or representative information, where lawful and necessary.

Check configured authoritative public sources for:
- Sanctions-related matches.
- Restricted-party matches.
- Official regulatory notices.
- Public business registration information.
- Credible adverse-media findings requiring review.

Keep official sanctions-list matches separate from ordinary news reports.

## 10.2 Trade Screening

After the Buyer enters preliminary Trade Request details, assess the proposed goods and route.

Collect:
- Product description.
- Product category.
- HS code, if known.
- Quantity and unit.
- Country of origin.
- Destination country.
- Transit countries or route, where known.
- Proposed end use.
- End user, where relevant.
- Licences and permits, where applicable.

Suggested official source registry:

- UN Security Council Consolidated Sanctions List.
- US OFAC Sanctions List Service.
- UK Sanctions List.
- EU consolidated financial sanctions information.
- US BIS Consolidated Screening List.
- Indian DGFT import/export policy.
- Indian DGFT SCOMET controls.
- Other relevant official national trade-control sources.

Use jurisdiction-appropriate sources.

Record source name, URL, authority, date checked, update date where available, matched entry and evidence reference.

Do not rely only on general web search results.

Do not treat an AI-suggested HS code as an official customs classification.

## 10.3 Screening Results

Use:

- CLEAR_ON_CHECKED_SOURCES.
- POTENTIAL_MATCH_REVIEW_REQUIRED.
- RESTRICTED_LICENCE_REVIEW.
- PROHIBITED_OR_SANCTIONS_ALERT.
- INCONCLUSIVE.
- SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE.

An unavailable or inconclusive source must never result in an automatic clear status.

## 10.4 AI Review Rules

AI may:
- Summarize findings.
- Compare relevant company identifiers.
- Explain possible matches.
- Identify missing information.
- Suggest whether manual review is required.

AI must not:
- Declare a company illegal from a name-only match.
- Automatically approve a high-risk case.
- Treat the absence of search results as proof of compliance.
- Make an irreversible legal decision.

Potential matches and high-risk issues must go into the internal Admin Review Queue.

Admin decisions must include evidence references, reason, reviewer identity and timestamp.

Clearly label simulated hackathon screening results as DEMO / SIMULATED.

